-- title:
--   Tameness of cusp pole orders on the ℓ-degeneracy roof
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number and $\ell$ a prime, and assume $(N : K) \ne 0$, $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$. Write $j(\mathsf q) =$ `jqModC K` for the Laurent series over $K$ obtained from the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and $j(\mathsf q^{M}) =$ `jqNModC K M` for its image under the substitution $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{M}$ (`qExpand K M`). Let $y$ be a place of `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $K$ generated by $j(\mathsf q)$, $j(\mathsf q^{N})$, $j(\mathsf q^{\ell})$ and $j(\mathsf q^{N\ell})$ over $K$ — that is, a valuation subring containing $K$, different from the whole field and a principal ideal ring — with associated integer-valued order function $\operatorname{ord}_y$. Suppose that $\operatorname{ord}_y$ of the image of $j(\mathsf q)$ under `heckeAlphaC` (the inclusion of $K(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{N}))$ into the roof) is negative. Then the absolute values of $\operatorname{ord}_y\bigl(j(\mathsf q)\bigr)$ and of $\operatorname{ord}_y\bigl(j(\mathsf q^{\ell})\bigr)$, the latter being the image of $j(\mathsf q)$ under `heckeBetaC` (the map induced by $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{\ell}$), are both non-zero in $K$, i.e. both pole orders are prime to $p$.
--
--   The assertion is that the pole orders at a cusp of the $\ell$-degeneracy roof, which up to factors $\ell^{\pm 1}$ are the widths of the cusps of $X_0(N\ell)$ and hence divide a power of $N\ell$, are prime to the characteristic. It supplies the tameness input at cusps for the Hecke correspondence computations, and is used in [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.trace_heckeBetaC_mul_pow_mem_riemannRochSpace_weightDivisor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.trace_heckeBetaC_mul_pow_mem_riemannRochSpace_weightDivisor).
